**(c) Implemented-but-wrong:**

- The commit's claim that `@radix-ui/react-accordion` and `@radix-ui/react-collapsible` "remain in package.json as transitive needs of `@fumadocs/base-ui`'s own native Accordion/Collapsible" is **false**, independently verified: `@fumadocs/base-ui/package.json` lists only `@base-ui/react` as a dependency — no Radix packages at all — and `pnpm why` confirms both packages resolve as **direct** dependencies of the root `package.json`, not transitive from anything. They are orphaned, fully-unused direct dependencies post-migration, mischaracterized in the one commit whose explicit purpose is confirming Radix retirement "not as an assumption." Everything else checks out (Accordion `id`→CopyButton, Banner `id`/`variant`, Cards `href`/`title`, Tabs wiring, Slide/Illu slugs all resolve to real on-disk images).

**Summary:** Standards axis — 0 hard violations, 3 minor judgement-call smells (worst: duplicated Tabs block, arguably necessary for the demo). Spec axis — 2 partial/missing ACs (`pnpm build` unverified, manual browser smoke check substituted with static reasoning) and 1 implemented-but-wrong finding (worst: the commit's factually incorrect claim that the leftover Radix packages are transitive, when they're actually direct, unused dependencies — a real miss in a ticket whose entire point was verifying Radix retirement by search rather than assumption).

